{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And you shall sanctify them today and tomorrow.</b> This sanctification is that a man not approach a woman, and also that they separate themselves from all impurity, for one who guards himself from impurity is called holy." "<b>And they shall wash their garments.</b> From the washing of garments we learn the immersion of the body, and so the Rabbis of blessed memory expounded in the Mekhilta: there is no washing of garments that does not require immersion."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:03.060239968Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}